handleRequest -- handle a JSON-RPC request
******************************************

  * Usage: 
        handleRequest(server, str)
  * Inputs:
      * server, a *note JSON-RPC server: JSONRPCServer,, 
      * str, a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, a JSON-RPC 2.0 request
        object;
  * Outputs:
      * a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String, or *note null:
        (Macaulay2Doc)null,, the response to the request or null if the request
        was a notification

Description
===========

This method processes an incoming JSON-RPC request. It takes a JSON-encoded
string representing a request (or batch of requests) and returns the
corresponding JSON-RPC response. It handles method invocation, error handling,
and batching automatically.  Note that *note makeRequest: makeRequest, is
useful for constructing requests.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : server = new JSONRPCServer                                              |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = server                                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : JSONRPCServer                                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : registerMethod(server, "sum", plus)                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : handleRequest(server, makeRequest("sum", {2, 3}, 1))                    |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = {"result": 5, "jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1}                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : handleRequest(server, makeRequest({("sum", {4, 5}, 2), ("sum", {6, 7},  |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = [{"result": 9, "jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 2}, {"result": 13, "jsonrpc":    |
|     "2.0", "id": 3}]                                                        |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|3)}))                                                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

If you need to do any error handling in a method, then the *note JSONRPCError:
JSONRPCError, class may be useful.

* Menu:

* JSONRPCError::                class for JSON-RPC errors

Ways to use handleRequest:
==========================

  * "handleRequest(JSONRPCServer,String)"

