JSONRPCError -- class for JSON-RPC errors
*****************************************

  * Usage: 
        JSONRPCError(errCode, msg, data)
        JSONRPCError(errCode, msg)
  * Inputs:
      * errCode, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
      * msg, a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, 
      * data, a *note thing: (Macaulay2Doc)Thing,, 

Description
===========

This class is used to represent errors that occur during the processing of
JSON-RPC requests. It provides a structured way to format error responses,
including an error code, message, and optional additional data. This class
ensures that errors are properly formatted according to the JSON-RPC 2.0
specification and can be easily included in responses to clients.

+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : server = new JSONRPCServer                                           |
|                                                                          |
|o1 = server                                                               |
|                                                                          |
|o1 : JSONRPCServer                                                        |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : registerMethod(server, "divide", (x, y) -> (                         |
|             if zero y then JSONRPCError(-32001, "division by zero")      |
|             else x/y))                                                   |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : handleRequest(server, makeRequest("divide", {1, 0}, 1))              |
|                                                                          |
|o3 = {"error": {"code": -32001, "message": "division by zero"}, "jsonrpc":|
|     "2.0", "id": 1}                                                      |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : handleRequest(server, makeRequest("divide", {22, 7}, 2))             |
|                                                                          |
|o4 = {"result": 3.142857142857143, "jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 2}             |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Note that the error codes -32000 to -32099 are reserved for use by JSON-RPC
servers, so errCode should lie in this interval (although this isn't checked).

