makeRequest -- construct a JSON-RPC request
*******************************************

  * Usage: 
        makeRequest(m, params, ID)
  * Inputs:
      * m, a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, method name; 
      * params, a *note hash table: (Macaulay2Doc)HashTable, or a *note list:
        (Macaulay2Doc)List,, method parameters (optional);
      * ID, a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String, or an *note integer:
        (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, id (if omitted, then the request is a notification);
  * Outputs:
      * a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, JSON-RPC request object; 

Description
===========

This method constructs a JSON-RPC request. The m parameter specifies the name
of the method being called, while params contains the arguments for the method
(if any). The optional ID parameter is used to correlate requests and
responses. This method generates a JSON-encoded string representing the
request, ready to be sent to the server. If no ID is provided, then the request
is a notification and the server will return nothing.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : makeRequest("foo", hashTable{"x" => 2, "y" => 3}, 1)                    |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = {"method": "foo", "id": 1, "jsonrpc": "2.0", "params": {"x": 2, "y": 3}}|
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : makeRequest("baz", {4, 5, 6}, 2)                                        |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = {"method": "baz", "id": 2, "jsonrpc": "2.0", "params": [4, 5, 6]}       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

When a list is given, its elements are expected to be sequences that can be
passed to *note makeRequest: makeRequest,.  The result is an array containing a
batch request.

+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : makeRequest({                                                        |
|             ("foo", hashTable{"x" => 7, "y" => 8}, 3),                   |
|             ("bar", {9, 10, 11}, 4)})                                    |
|                                                                          |
|o3 = [{"method": "foo", "id": 3, "jsonrpc": "2.0", "params": {"x": 7, "y":|
|     8}}, {"method": "bar", "id": 4, "jsonrpc": "2.0", "params": [9, 10,  |
|     11]}]                                                                |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+

